<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Exactly what this module's working code consumes today, all inward:

       TaxLogicEngine     the raw payload (T4RawInput/T4RawBox), T4BoxCodes, and
                          the existing ParseResult/ValidationError vocabulary;
       DocumentExtraction the existing envelope, its single fail-closed gate, the
                          existing ExtractionProvenance, and the ingress port
                          this module implements — no second envelope,
                          validator, or provenance record is declared anywhere;
       CaseProcessing     the existing T4 chain, reached only through
                          T4CaseProcessor.Process (added by T04, the first task
                          whose code names it);
       CaseReview         the existing fail-closed review assembler (added by
                          T05, the first task whose code names it);
       ClientIntake       the server-stored case and its document metadata,
                          read through IIntakeStore.FindAsync (added by T04, the
                          first task whose code names it);
       Tenancy            TrustedFirmId, so a content read cannot be handed a
                          route value, the opaque identifier source, the one
                          existing UTC-instant guard, and the one existing
                          retention authority.

       Nothing is pre-added for a later wave. The architecture's wider dependency
       set is real, but a reference no code names is an unused reference: the
       task that first consumes CaseReview adds it then, and sequential ownership
       of this file across waves is how that stays honest.

       Deliberately absent: Persistence, TaxAI.Portal, DocumentIntelligence, and
       every EF Core, ASP.NET Core, cloud, OCR, and LLM package. This module
       declares ports; infrastructure implements them. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\CaseProcessing\CaseProcessing.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\CaseReview\CaseReview.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\ClientIntake\ClientIntake.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\DocumentExtraction\DocumentExtraction.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\TaxLogicEngine\TaxLogicEngine.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Tenancy\Tenancy.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
